  "body": "If `server_name.yaml` is edited manually, the postinst overwrites it on upgrade. A few points:\r\n* if it's autogenerated, the file should say so\r\n* an upgrade shouldn't touch it anyway (the postinst can tell if it's an upgrade or a fresh install)\r\n* even on fresh install, if the file exists, maybe we should leave it alone?\r\n\r\nUpdate 2019/01/18: likewise, `report_stats.yaml` is also overwritten according to the debconf database. (In some ways this is worse, because it may be some time before the admin notices it.)",
